<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Extra Info.plist keys merged into the macOS bundle by the Tauri bundler.

  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription is NOT optional: macOS terminates an app that
  reaches for the microphone without it, and recording the microphone is the
  whole product. The string below is what the user reads in the permission
  prompt, so it says what we take and where it goes.

  Screen/system audio capture via getDisplayMedia (the webview fallback) is
  governed by the Screen Recording privacy setting, which macOS prompts for on
  first use and which has no Info.plist key — nothing to declare here for it.

  NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription is for the native path (src-tauri/src/audio,
  the `system-audio-tap` feature): Core Audio's process-tap API surfaces this
  string in its own permission prompt the first time a tap is created.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Ledgeur records meeting audio so it can transcribe it on this device. Audio and transcripts stay on your machine unless you choose to sync them.</string>
	<key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Ledgeur captures the meeting audio your Mac is playing so it can transcribe the other side of a call. Audio and transcripts stay on your machine unless you choose to sync them.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
